The introduction of a new method `commonSettings` in `AbstractChallengeRestTest` and its usage in subclasses like `StandardVersusLogsIndexModeChallengeRestIT` is clear and logical. However, the implementation of `commonSettings` in `StandardVersusLogsIndexModeChallengeRestIT` could be improved for better readability and maintainability.
### SUGGESTION
Consider extracting the logic inside `commonSettings` into a separate method to avoid code duplication and improve readability. For example:
```java
@Override
public void commonSettings(Settings.Builder builder) {
    applyRandomShardAndReplicaSettings(builder);
    builder.put("index.mapping.total_fields.limit", 5000);
}
private void applyRandomShardAndReplicaSettings(Settings.Builder builder) {
    if (numShards > 0) {
        builder.put("index.number_of_shards", numShards);
    }
    if (numReplicas > 0) {
        builder.put("index.number_of_replicas", numReplicas);
    }
}
```
This separation of concerns makes the code easier to understand and maintain.

